{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7L6Hj1kXS3SGd8z2pWN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft this, there's one problem to sort out and a few questions.\n\n**The \"same cleaner every single time\" promise.** What you've described is a regular cleaner plus a named backup, so you can't guarantee the same person every time. Last year about 4 in 10 customers had their cleaner change. Many of the people getting this email were in that group, and some left partly because of it. If the email promises \"every single time\" and then the backup shows up, you'll lose them again and they'll trust you less. I'd suggest promising what you actually offer: \"your own regular cleaner, plus one named backup you'll meet ahead of time, never a stranger.\" I think that's a strong offer and it's true. Does that work, or have you made changes since then that would let you promise more?\n\nA few more questions:\n\n1. **What happens after the $99 cleaning?** Does the price go back to $165? Is there any discount for returning customers, or any commitment they have to make, like a minimum number of visits or a contract? Price was the main reason people left, so they'll look for this first.\n2. **Has anything improved cleaner retention since last year?** For example, a raise, benefits, or lower turnover this year so far. That would back up the claim that \"your cleaner will stick around.\"\n3. **How does the backup work in practice?** Does the customer meet the backup or see their name and photo in advance? How often does the backup actually end up cleaning?\n4. **Do you have a deadline for the $99 offer?** And should it go out from you by name? A personal note from the owner usually works better for win-backs.\n5. **Is there anything else these customers might have run into?** Missed visits, damage claims, billing problems? I want the email to avoid making claims a former customer knows aren't true.\n\nIf you don't know some of these, that's fine. I'll write without them and won't fill in guesses."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":9533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":699},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad85ba34-1381-4e00-a8de-84d0f1e97ff7","uuid":"e5f18af3-df3e-4ec4-ac12-bfd380314570","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:38:24.276Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7L6HWd5fBjQY3uUZGY3"}
