{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7L7arRzeTamCWHGhEzj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written it around your wording: a regular cleaner plus a named backup. I left out \"meet them ahead of time\" and \"never a stranger\" because you don't know yet how the backup will work.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Your own cleaner, and $99 to come back\n\nHi [First name],\n\nWhen customers left Brightway last year, the two reasons we heard most were price and a different cleaner showing up too often. The second one was our fault, and we've changed how we work.\n\nSince July, every customer has their own regular cleaner, plus a named backup who comes if your cleaner is sick or on holiday. Since we made that change, 1 of our 18 cleaners has left.\n\nOn price, I'll be straight with you. We charge $165 for a 3-bedroom every other week, and the app services charge about $140. The difference pays for cleaners who are our employees, earning $21 an hour, with insurance on every visit.\n\nIf you'd like to come back, your first cleaning is $99. After that it's our regular price. There's no contract and you can cancel any time. This offer ends December 31.\n\nReply to this email or call [phone] to book.\n\nLisa Grant\nOwner, Brightway Home Cleaning\n</final_document>\n\nA few notes:\n- **Two blanks to fill in:** the customer's first name and your phone number.\n- **Length:** it's about 165 words. If you need to cut, the price paragraph could come down to one sentence. I'd keep it, though. Price was the main reason people left, so they'll be wondering about it, and comparing it with the apps yourself is more convincing than leaving it out.\n- **\"1 of 18 since July\":** that's only about four months. It's accurate, but if someone asks, don't present it as a full year's record.\n- **If you settle how the backup works:** for example, if customers get the backup's name and photo in advance, add that to the secon